'''''Euphorbia grandidens''''', commonly known as '''valleybush euphorbia''' or '''large-toothed euphorbia''', is a species of [[plant]] in the family [[Euphorbiaceae]] native to southern Africa.<ref>{{Cite web|url =http://pza.sanbi.org/euphorbia-grandidens |title = Euphorbia grandidens|website = Plantzafrica.com | publisher=South African National Biodiversity Institute |access-date = 1 January 2021 | first=Sifiso | last=Mnxati| date =August 2015}}</ref> While sometimes shrubby, it can also be a [[pachycaul]]ous tree up to {{convert|15|m}} tall, with the short horizontal branches  in a rosette at the top of the main trunk and reiterations. These horizontal branches are [[succulent]] and triangular in cross-section.<ref>{{cite book | last1= Turner | first1= R.J. Jr. | last2= Wasson |first2= Ernie | date=1999 | title= Botanica | location= not given | publisher= Barnes & Noble | page= 361 |ISBN= 0760716420 }}</ref>

